§ `Chapters 33 to 38 -- kydells, writs, measures and wardship`

§§ `Chapter 33 -- kydells`

-- gloss (not the text's): "kydell" is the text's word for a fixed fishing weir; whether a thing is
-- one, and where it stands, are taken as plain facts.  "For the future" is read as from the
-- moment of the grant, so no date is asked.
-- src:73 | All kydells for the future shall be removed altogether from Thames and Medway, and throughout all England, except upon the sea coast.
@ref Chapter 33 (src:73)
GIVEN `the kydell is in England` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kydell is upon the sea coast` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `ch 33 -- the kydell is to be removed` IS
    IF `the kydell is in England`
    THEN IF `the kydell is upon the sea coast`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except upon the sea coast".
         THEN `Not obliged`
         ELSE Obliged
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: except because "except" carves the sea coast out of the duty; the branch is reached by a kydell not in England, which the sentence does not name).
    ELSE `Obligation not covered`

§§ `Chapter 34 -- the writ praecipe`

-- src:75 | The writ which is called praecipe shall not for the future be issued to anyone, concerning any tenement whereby a freeman may lose his court.
@ref Chapter 34 (src:75)
GIVEN `the writ is the writ called praecipe` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writ concerns a tenement whereby a freeman may lose his court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 34 -- the writ praecipe may be issued` IS
    IF   `the writ is the writ called praecipe`
     AND `the writ concerns a tenement whereby a freeman may lose his court`
    THEN Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 35 -- measures and weights`

-- The text says "one measure" of wine and of ale without fixing its size; for corn it names the
-- London quarter, for cloth a width of two ells within the selvedges, and for weights it says
-- "as of measures".  Whether a weight is one standard is read from "as of measures" (fork F35).
-- src:77 | Let there be one measure of wine throughout our whole realm;
-- src:77 | and one measure of ale;
-- src:77 | and one measure of corn, to wit, “the London quarter”;
-- src:77 | and one width of cloth (whether dyed, or russet, or halberget), to wit, two ells within the selvedges;
-- src:77 | of weights also let it be as of measures.
@ref Chapter 35 (src:77)
GIVEN thing IS A Commodity
GIVETH A Standard
DECIDE `ch 35 -- the standard throughout the realm` IS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `wine`  THEN `one measure, whose size the text does not state`
    WHEN `ale`   THEN `one measure, whose size the text does not state`
    WHEN `corn`  THEN `the London quarter`
    WHEN `cloth, whether dyed, or russet, or halberget` THEN `two ells within the selvedges`
    WHEN `a weight` THEN `one weight, whose size the text does not state`
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the cases above and does not close the list with "only".
    OTHERWISE `Standard not covered`

-- src:77 | Let there be one measure of wine throughout our whole realm;
-- src:77 | and one measure of ale;
-- src:77 | and one measure of corn, to wit, “the London quarter”;
-- src:77 | and one width of cloth (whether dyed, or russet, or halberget), to wit, two ells within the selvedges;
-- src:77 | of weights also let it be as of measures.
@ref Chapter 35 (src:77)
GIVEN thing IS A Commodity
      `the sale is within the realm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure used differs from the standard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 35 -- a measure other than the standard may be used` IS
    IF `the sale is within the realm`
    THEN IF `ch 35 -- the standard throughout the realm` thing EQUALS `Standard not covered`
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
         THEN `Bar not covered`
         ELSE IF `the measure used differs from the standard`
              THEN Barred
              -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "one measure" states the single standard; it does not say that using it is allowed (F64c).
              ELSE `Bar not covered`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 36 -- the writ of inquisition of life or limbs`

